CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ sizeof\.\.\. of a 1-element non-type pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ sizeof\.\.\. of a 2-element non-type pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ sizeof\.\.\. of a 3-element non-type pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ non-type value pack Trait<Us>::value\.\.\. forwarded and counted: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
N5008 [expr.sizeof]/5 + [temp.variadic]/8.  `sizeof...(P)` counts the pack's
elements regardless of whether P is a type or a NON-type parameter pack.  CBMC's
parser stored a non-type pack's name as the sizeof operand (type-checked as a
value before the pack-count logic ran), so `box<N...>::n == sizeof...(Vs)` was
wrong for a non-type pack of every arity; a type pack was unaffected.  Fixed by
storing the non-type pack's name in ID_type_arg so both forms take the
pack-counting path.  Non-vacuous: the three direct assertions depend on the pack
arity (1/2/3).  The forwarded-pack case (`box<sz<Us>::v...>::n` in a function
template) is the shape that first surfaced this.
